Fix GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c (CVE-2026-84383): heap-based buffer overflow (CWE-122)
in the libheif AVIF/HEIF decoder bundled by sharp via sharp-libvips.

Upstream sharp v0.35.4 fixes this by upgrading the bundled sharp-libvips to
v1.3.3, which vendors libvips 8.18.6 / libheif 1.23.2. The vulnerable code
lives entirely inside the vendored native dependency, so the sharp-side fix is
a version-pointer bump of the per-platform native addon (@img/sharp-*) and the
vendored libvips runtime (@img/sharp-libvips-*), together with the compile-time
libvips version guard.

This backport to 0.35.0 mirrors the accepted sibling patches for 0.34.5 and
0.35.3 (same GHSA, same version-pointer fix pattern):
  * @img/sharp-*            0.35.0 -> 0.35.4  (native addon relinked against
                                               libvips-cpp.so.8.18.6)
  * @img/sharp-libvips-*    1.3.0  -> 1.3.3   (vendored libvips 8.18.6 /
                                               libheif 1.23.2)
  * config.libvips          >=8.18.3 -> >=8.18.6
  * src/common.h guard      8.18.3   -> 8.18.6

Keeping the native addon (@img/sharp-*) and the vendored libvips runtime
(@img/sharp-libvips-*) pinned to matching fixed versions preserves the
DT_NEEDED linkage (addon 0.35.4 links libvips-cpp.so.8.18.6, shipped by
sharp-libvips 1.3.3), which is required for the fix to actually load and take
effect at runtime.

